      "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nFix precision loss when converting string tool arguments to schema-declared integers in the response-template parser.\n\n## Details\n\nThe integer fallback previously converted strings through `float()`, which could round large values or small fractions. For example, `9223372036854775807.0` could become `9223372036854775808`, while `1e-400` could become `0`.\n\nUse `Decimal` to check whether the original value is integral and convert it to an integer without losing precision. Keep the existing float-based validation and fallback behavior for unsupported values.\n\n## Validation\n\nAdded one regression test with six cases covering large integers, scientific notation, fractional values, underflow, overflow, and extreme exponents.\n\n- Before: **5 regression subcases failed**.\n- After: **147 tests passed**.\n- All applicable pre-commit hooks passed.\n- Manually verified streaming and non-streaming parsing with the existing Gemma4 response template.\n\n```bash\n.venv/bin/python -m pytest \\\n  --confcutdir=tests/parser \\\n  tests/parser/test_chat_parsing.py \\\n  tests/parser/test_response_template.py -q\n\npre-commit run --files \\\n  vllm/parser/chat_parsing/response_parser.py \\\n  tests/parser/test_chat_parsing.py\n```\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Pull Request Checklist</summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Keeps the change within the existing coercion function.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Parser tests and streaming checks passed.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Passes applicable pre-commit checks.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes the root cause, fix, and regression tests.\n\n</details>",
